Subject: empty the ring buffer when the transport seeks

In transport mode (-t), a locate or a start was served by moving the file
position only. The ring buffer still held the audio read before the seek, so
the program first played that audio, then jumped to the new position: after a
start from 0, the first 4096 samples were heard twice (more with -b).

While a seek is pending the process thread now writes silence and leaves the
ring buffer alone. The disk thread seeks, empties the ring buffer, fills it
again and only then clears the request, so the process thread resumes with the
right audio. The converter is reset in sync_handler(), which runs in the
process thread. The request is read and cleared with atomic operations, and a
request that arrives while one is being served is not lost.

Tested with a ramp: the signal used to fall back to 0 after 0.1 s (0.36 s with
-b 16384) and is now monotonic from the start.
--- a/cmd/rju-play.c
+++ b/cmd/rju-play.c
@@ -65,27 +65,61 @@
